CLASS: CONTRACT
Last updated: 2026-08-24

# Main crate contract

The main `egglog` crate has the source code under `./src/` and is concerned with parsing, desugaring, proofs, type checking, and lowering.

Start with `src/lib.md` for the language and Rust API entry points. The `src/sort/add_primitive` package owns the `egglog-add-primitive` procedural macro; backing database implementation lives in `core-relations`, and its main-crate adapter lives in `egglog-bridge`.

## Architecture and decision index

| record | body |
| --- | --- |
| term and proof encoding | src/proofs/proof_encoding.md |

The indexed record is the single home for its full architecture text; this contract only makes it reachable.
CLASS: CONTRACT
Last updated: 2026-08-24

# Core relations contract

`core-relations` is the backing database implementation. It supports both parallel and serial modes. By default, it runs in serial mode and uses only a single thread.

Concurrency primitives live in `concurrency`, identifiers live in `numeric-id`, union-find storage lives in `union-find`, and main-crate adaptation lives in `egglog-bridge`.

Repository lint and test enforcement is defined by `Makefile`, `clippy.toml`, and `.config/nextest.toml`.
CLASS: CONTRACT
Last updated: 2026-08-24

# Bridge contract

`egglog-bridge` is the bridge between the main crate and the core-relations, and provides abstractions/utility for rules, union-find, rows, etc.

The database implementation remains owned by `core-relations`; language parsing, desugaring, proofs, type checking, and lowering remain owned by `src`.

Use the shared enforcement sources at `Makefile`, `clippy.toml`, and `.config/nextest.toml`.
CLASS: CONTRACT
Last updated: 2026-08-24

# Test corpus contract

The `tests` folder contains a list of example egglog programs.

`tests/fail-typecheck` owns programs expected to fail type checking, `tests/pass-typecheck` owns programs expected to pass it, `tests/header` owns shared input headers, `tests/proofs` owns proof examples, and `tests/web-demo` owns browser-demo fixtures. Snapshot output lives in `tests/snapshots` and is regenerated through the repository's test harness rather than edited as independent source.

Repository test ordering and enforcement is defined by `Makefile` and `.config/nextest.toml`.

